            "body": "**Blast radius** is a borrowed term: if something explodes, how big is the crater? In cloud security it means — if one credential, server, or account is compromised, how much can the attacker reach? The goal of good architecture is to keep that crater **small**. Analogy: a ship with **watertight compartments** — a hull breach floods one compartment, not the whole ship, so it stays afloat. Worked example: if your entire company runs in one AWS account and one role gets stolen, the attacker may touch everything. Split into compartments and a breach is contained. Everything in this topic is a way to build watertight walls.",
