        "week": 1,
        "description": "The same cloud diagram tells two stories: a defender sees controls to maintain, an attacker sees a path to the data. This topic teaches you to read one architecture twice — enumerating identities, entry points and trust relationships — so you can map the route from the internet all the way to sensitive data, then flip each attacker step into a defense that would cut it. Learning to switch perspectives is the core skill of cloud security.",
