            "title": "One diagram, two stories",
            "body": "Hand the same architecture diagram to a defender and an attacker and they see different things. The **defender** lists controls: 'this bucket is encrypted, that firewall blocks port 22, logging is on'. The **attacker** lists opportunities: 'that server faces the internet, it has a role that can read the database, nothing stops it reaching storage'. Analogy: a locksmith and a burglar look at the same door — one checks the lock quality, the other checks whether it's actually locked. Learning to **toggle** between these views is the master skill: you can't defend a path you've never traced as an attacker.",
