        "description": "Every action in a cloud account is taken by some identity the platform calls a 'principal.' Before you can reason about who can break into an account, you need to know the kinds of identities that exist and why workloads should use short-lived role credentials instead of permanent keys. This topic builds that foundation from zero.",
