            "title": "Whoami first: get-caller-identity",
            "body": "Before touching anything, answer the most basic question: *who is this credential?* **`aws sts get-caller-identity`** returns the **Account ID**, the **user or role ARN**, and a unique ID. It is read-only and the single safest first call. Analogy: you have found a keycard, so before wandering the building you check whose badge it is and which company issued it. Worked example output includes `Arn: arn:aws:iam::123456789012:user/deploy-bot`, telling you this is an IAM *user* named `deploy-bot` in that account. The ARN shape (`user/` versus `assumed-role/`) immediately tells you whether you are a user or an assumed role.",
