            "body": "Managed policies keep up to five **versions**, and one is marked default (active). Two primitives abuse this. `iam:CreatePolicyVersion` with `--set-as-default` writes a new admin-granting version of a policy you are attached to — instantly widening your rights. `iam:SetDefaultPolicyVersion` is subtler: if an *old, unused* version of the policy was more permissive, you simply flip the default back to it without creating anything new. Analogy: a policy is a rulebook with past editions still on the shelf; `SetDefaultPolicyVersion` says 'let's go back to the 2019 edition that let everyone in.' Predict: does `SetDefaultPolicyVersion` need `CreatePolicyVersion` too? ||No — if a permissive old version already exists, flipping the default is enough on its own.||",
