            "title": "Why PassRole alone does nothing",
            "body": "`iam:PassRole` is inert by itself — it is not an action you can 'run' to get credentials. It only has meaning when paired with a **service-creating action** that accepts a role: `lambda:CreateFunction`, `ec2:RunInstances`, `glue:CreateDevEndpoint`, `cloudformation:CreateStack`, and others. This is why a policy granting `iam:PassRole` on `Resource: *` is a red flag only when the principal *also* holds one of those service actions. Analogy: a valet ticket is useless unless there is a valet on duty willing to fetch a car. Predict: if a user has `iam:PassRole` but no compute-creating action, can they escalate via PassRole? ||No — there is no service to assume the role, so the primitive is dead. Look for the paired action.||",
