            "title": "Sink 2 — EC2 instance profiles + metadata",
            "body": "With `iam:PassRole` + `ec2:RunInstances` (and an existing **instance profile** wrapping a privileged role), you launch an instance attached to that profile, then read its temporary credentials from the **Instance Metadata Service** at `169.254.169.254`. On IMDSv1 that is a plain GET to `/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/<role-name>`. (This is the exact mechanism behind the 2019 **Capital One** breach, where an SSRF reached IMDSv1 and pulled a role's credentials to read S3.) Analogy: you rent a company car that comes with the keys to HQ in the glovebox. Note: an instance profile is the wrapper EC2 needs — a bare role ARN will not attach.",
