        "description": "A role is a set of permissions that anyone on its 'guest list' can borrow — and that guest list is the trust policy. If the guest list is written too loosely, attackers invite themselves in without touching your permissions at all. This topic teaches you to read trust policies like an attacker and spot the gaps that let the wrong people assume powerful roles.",
