            "title": "Two sides grant access, not one",
            "body": "AWS authorization has two independent sources. **Identity policies** attach to a user/role and say 'this principal may do X'. **Resource policies** attach to the resource (an S3 bucket, a KMS key, a Lambda, an SQS queue) and say 'these principals may touch ME'. For most cross-account access, allow on *either* side can be enough — and resource policies can reach principals in *other accounts* directly. Analogy: identity policy is your employee badge's clearance; a resource policy is a sign on a specific door saying 'Bob from the other building may also enter here.' Beginners audit only badges and miss the door signs entirely.",
