        "title": "Persistence via Identity",
        "type": "lab",
        "week": 2,
        "description": "Getting admin once is loud and temporary; staying admin quietly is the attacker's real goal. In AWS, persistence means planting durable ways back in using identities, trust, and event triggers — and every technique leaves a specific trace in the logs. This topic teaches both the plant and the detection, so you understand each move from both sides.",
