            "title": "Plant 3 — a backdoor role with wide trust",
            "body": "More subtle than a user: create (or repurpose) a **role** with admin permissions and a **trust policy** that names an account or principal the attacker controls — or `\"Principal\": {\"AWS\": \"*\"}`. Later, from anywhere, the attacker just runs `sts:AssumeRole` and is admin again, leaving behind no long-lived keys to rotate. Analogy: instead of copying a key you install a new door that only your remote opens — nothing on the victim's keyring to change. Forensic footprint: **`CreateRole`** / **`UpdateAssumeRolePolicy`** events where the new trust names an external account or a wildcard. Detection: alert when any trust policy is widened, and flag roles trusting accounts outside your Organization.",
