            "title": "Condition keys — MFA, SourceIp, PrincipalOrgID",
            "body": "**Condition keys** add situational requirements to sensitive actions. `aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent = true` forces MFA before an escalation-prone action runs. `aws:SourceIp` restricts sensitive calls to your corporate/VPN ranges. `aws:PrincipalOrgID` ensures only identities inside your Organization can assume a role or touch a resource, even if an ARN leaks. Analogy: the vault door now also requires a fingerprint, that you are standing in the right building, and a company badge — not just the key. Worked example: wrap `iam:*` admin actions in `\"Condition\": {\"Bool\": {\"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent\": \"true\"}}` so a stolen key without MFA cannot escalate. Predict: does MFA-on-action help against a stolen long-term access key? ||Yes — a key alone lacks an MFA session, so MFA-conditioned actions fail, blunting key theft.||",
