        "type": "theory",
        "week": 2,
        "description": "A pre-signed URL is a special link that grants time-limited access to a private object without the recipient needing any AWS credentials. It is enormously useful for sharing files, but because the permission is baked into the link itself, it is frequently misused and leaked. This lesson shows exactly how they are abused and how to bound them safely.",
