            "title": "Map every exit before you defend",
            "body": "Good defence starts by listing *every* way data can leave, because you only need to miss one. For a bucket the main egress paths are: **public read** (anonymous `GetObject`), a **leaked pre-signed URL**, **replication** to another region or account, a **shared snapshot or export**, and **over-broad IAM** letting too many identities read. Analogy: securing a warehouse means checking every door, loading bay, window, and ventilation duct — not just the front entrance. Worked example: a team hardens the bucket policy but forgets replication is quietly copying objects to a second account — the data still leaves. Enumerate the paths first, then you can assign a control to each.",
