        "description": "The root cause of most credential leaks is long-lived static keys sitting somewhere an attacker can find them. This topic teaches the modern alternative: workloads prove their identity to the cloud and receive short-lived credentials automatically, so there is no key to steal. You'll understand instance profiles, IRSA, and OIDC federation, and why they kill the leaked-key problem at its source.",
