            "title": "EC2 instance profiles & ECS task roles",
            "body": "On AWS compute, the first step away from static keys is attaching a **role** to the workload. An **EC2 instance profile** or **ECS task role** tells AWS 'this machine *is* this role,' and the platform delivers **temporary credentials** to the instance metadata service, rotating them automatically every few hours. Your code uses the SDK's default credential chain and never sees a stored key. The trade-off is that whatever can reach the metadata endpoint can use those credentials — which is exactly why **IMDSv2** (token-required, hop-limited) matters, and why the role should carry only the permissions that one workload needs. Worked example: an app on EC2 calls S3 with no credentials in its config at all; the SDK silently pulls them from `169.254.169.254`.",
