        "type": "theory",
        "week": 3,
        "description": "Every cloud server has a hidden helper it can talk to at one special address, and that helper will hand out the server's own cloud credentials. This single service is the reason a web bug can turn into a full cloud-account compromise. Understand exactly what it serves and how, and the rest of this module falls into place.",
