        "description": "A breach almost never stops at the first server. Once an attacker has one foothold, the real damage comes from spreading sideways to reach databases, secrets and admin systems. This topic shows how flat networks and permissive internal rules turn a single compromise into an account-wide one — and sets up the segmentation that stops it.",
