            "title": "North-South vs East-West",
            "body": "Network traffic splits into two directions. **North-south** is traffic between the internet and your systems (a user hitting your web server). **East-west** is traffic *between* your internal systems (the web server talking to the database). Most defenses obsess over north-south — the perimeter firewall — while east-west inside the network is wide open. Analogy: a building with a tough front-door guard but no interior locks; once a thief is in the lobby, every floor is a free stroll. **Lateral movement** is the attacker's east-west journey from their entry point to the real prize.",
