            "title": "No Server, Still a Target",
            "body": "**Serverless** (also called **FaaS**, Function-as-a-Service, like **AWS Lambda**) means you hand the cloud a chunk of code and it runs that code only when something triggers it, then throws the environment away. There is no machine you SSH into, no OS to patch, no long-running process. **Analogy:** it is a pop-up food stall the city assembles for 200 milliseconds when an order arrives and dismantles right after. You never own the stall, but you still own the recipe, the ingredients delivered to it, and the keys it carries. Those three things, plus the code itself, are what an attacker goes after."
