        "type": "theory",
        "week": 3,
        "description": "Your function ships with every library it imports, and those libraries run with your function's role. A single malicious or vulnerable package, pulled in at build time, becomes code execution in your account. This lesson explains how bad packages get in (typosquatting, dependency confusion, compromised maintainers) and how to scan, pin, and verify what you ship.",
