            "title": "You Ship More Than Your Code",
            "body": "When you package a function, its dependency **tree** comes along: the libraries you chose, plus every library *those* pull in, often dozens you never named. On Lambda they ride in the deployment bundle or in a **layer**, and all of it executes with the function's role. **Analogy:** you hired one contractor, but they brought a crew of subcontractors you never interviewed, and they all have keys to the building. The size of that uninspected crew is why supply-chain risk is not a side issue, it is often the largest body of code in your function."
