            "title": "Typosquatting and Malicious Packages",
            "body": "Attackers publish packages whose names are near-misses of popular ones, hoping a developer fat-fingers the name, this is **typosquatting** (e.g. a name one letter off from a widely-used library). Install the wrong one and its install script or imported code runs on your build machine and ships into your function. A famous real case was the **event-stream** incident (2018), where a widely-depended-on npm package was taken over by a new maintainer who slipped in code targeting a specific crypto wallet app. **Rule:** verify package names exactly and review new or recently-transferred dependencies before adding them.",
