            "title": "Scan in CI, Before It Ships",
            "body": "You cannot eyeball a tree of hundreds of packages, so automate it. Run a dependency scanner in your **CI pipeline** on every build: tools like **`npm audit`**, **Snyk**, and **Trivy** (which can scan the bundle and container-style layers) compare your locked versions against vulnerability databases and fail the build on serious findings. **Worked example:** CI runs `npm audit --audit-level=high` and `trivy fs ./bundle`; a high-severity transitive dependency blocks the deploy until it is upgraded. **Rule:** a scan that runs only on your laptop, occasionally, is not a control; it must gate the pipeline."
