        "type": "lab",
        "week": 3,
        "description": "Inside a Kubernetes cluster, identity and permissions are governed by RBAC — Role-Based Access Control — which decides which users and service accounts can do what. Just like over-broad IAM in a cloud account, over-broad RBAC combined with those auto-mounted tokens is the single most common way attackers escalate from a foothold to cluster admin. This topic teaches RBAC from scratch and then walks the real escalation paths that turn a small grant into full control.",
