            "title": "Escalation path: pods/exec and secrets",
            "body": "A common chain: you compromise a pod whose SA can `get secrets` and `create`/`exec` pods in its namespace. You list secrets to grab other credentials, and you `exec` into higher-value pods to steal their tokens. **Analogy:** a junior employee whose badge happens to open the records room and let them borrow colleagues' badges — small on paper, huge in practice. **Worked example:** `kubectl auth can-i --list` run with the stolen token reveals exactly these permissions, and `kubectl get secrets -o yaml` dumps them. The lesson: a seemingly minor SA permission can be the first link in a full compromise.",
