            "title": "Impersonate and bind: minting your own power",
            "body": "Two subtle but severe verbs: **`impersonate`** lets a subject send requests *as* another user/group/SA — so impersonating `system:masters` is instant admin. **`bind`** (and **`escalate`**) let you create a binding to a role more powerful than you currently hold, normally forbidden to stop self-promotion. **Analogy:** `impersonate` is a disguise that fools the checkpoint; `bind` is the authority to write your own promotion letter. **Takeaway:** audit for any non-admin subject holding `impersonate`, `bind`, or `escalate` — these are near-equivalent to cluster-admin and are easy to grant by accident in a broad ClusterRole.",
