        "description": "RBAC controls who can talk to the Kubernetes API, but once pods are running you also need guardrails on what those pods can do and who they can talk to at runtime. This topic covers the three big runtime controls: restricting dangerous pod settings, segmenting pod-to-pod network traffic, and protecting cluster secrets — plus the policy engines that enforce them automatically. These are the walls between your workloads when one of them is breached.",
