        "description": "In AWS almost everything happens through an API call — creating a user, reading a file, launching a server. CloudTrail is the service that writes down every one of those calls, so it is the single best record of who did what, from where, and when. Learn to read it and you can reconstruct an entire attack; if an attacker turns it off, they try to erase their tracks.",
