        "description": "In the cloud you don't own servers in a room — you own thousands of settings (a bucket that's public or private, a port open or closed, encryption on or off), and any one wrong setting can leak data. Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM) is the practice of continuously reading all those settings and comparing them to what 'good' looks like, so misconfigurations are found before attackers find them. This topic teaches you to run real CSPM tools and, crucially, to turn a flood of findings into the handful that actually matter.",
