        "description": "CSPM tells you *something* is wrong, but 'wrong' needs a definition everyone agrees on. The CIS Benchmarks are the industry's consensus checklist for how a cloud account should be hardened — written by practitioners, referenced by auditors, and built into most tools. This topic teaches the structure of the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark, the few controls that matter most, and how to continuously enforce them so your accounts don't quietly drift back into insecurity.",
