        "description": "Detecting a misconfiguration after it exists is good; making it *impossible to create* is better. Preventative guardrails flip security from 'find and fix' to 'can't happen in the first place'. This topic teaches the main tools — Service Control Policies, policy-as-code, and pre-deploy scanning — and the crucial distinction between stopping a bad action, bounding permissions, and merely detecting afterward.",
