            "title": "The hierarchy that leaks permissions downward",
            "body": "GCP arranges everything in a tree: **Organization -> Folders -> Projects -> Resources**. An IAM grant at a higher node is **inherited** by everything beneath it. Analogy: a company org chart where a rule pinned at HQ applies to every regional office and desk below it automatically. Worked example: grant `roles/viewer` to a user at the organization node and they can view resources in every project in the org, forever, until removed. Predict: if someone is Editor at the folder level, do they have Editor on projects created in that folder next year? ||Yes. Inheritance is dynamic, so new projects under that folder automatically inherit the folder-level binding.||",
