            "title": "A full GCP chain",
            "body": "Putting it together: (1) SSRF on a GCE-hosted app. (2) Hit the metadata server with `Metadata-Flavor: Google` to get a token for the **default Compute Engine SA**, often `Editor`. (3) With Editor, enumerate and find a more powerful SA you can `actAs` or `getAccessToken`. (4) Impersonate it. (5) Use its `setIamPolicy` to add yourself as project **Owner**. (6) Read every GCS bucket. Analogy: window (SSRF) -> glovebox master key (metadata) -> borrow a bigger badge (impersonation) -> rewrite the access list (setIamPolicy) -> open every unit. Each link is a separate, fixable control.",
